{"title":"Supply is elastic, installment #1637","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/970913897/0/marginalrevolution~Supply-is-elastic-installment.html","date":1790962357000,"content":"<p>For taxes too:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p><span>Using administrative data from Scandinavian countries, we provide evidence on international migration responses to wealth taxes and evaluate their aggregate economic implications. We find significant migration responses among the wealthy: A 1 percentage point increase in the top wealth tax rate decreases the stock of wealthy taxpayers by about 2 percent. A large fraction of the wealthy are business owners, and their businesses are negatively affected by owner out-migration. The aggregate effects are nevertheless modest: The migration responses to a 1 percentage point increase in the top wealth tax rate reduce employment by 0.02 percent, investments by 0.07 percent, and value added by 0.10 percent.</span></p></blockquote>\r\n<p>That is by Katrine Jakobsen, Henrik Kleven, Jonas Kolsrud, Camille Landais and Mathilde Munoz, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.aeaweb.org/articles/pdf/doi/10.1257/aer.20241596?etoc=1&amp;PHPSESSID=79b72da60309d4518a8b4f3a64624ec8&amp;legal-banner-cookie=yes&amp;_ga=GA1.2.1159893196.1790873484&amp;_gid=GA1.2.635361536.1790873484&amp;_ga_96K6S9DJLT=GS2.1.s1790873484%24o1%24g0%24t1790873523%24j21%24l0%24h0\" target=\"_blank\">in the latest issue of the AER</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/supply-is-elastic-installment-1637-2.html\">Supply is elastic, installment #1637</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/970913897/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.